# Jobs

- `jobs.Runner.Start(ctx, kind, Subject{Type, ID}, createdBy, fn)` persists a queued job, creates `logs/jobs/<id>.log` (0600) and runs `fn(ctx, log)` on a bounded worker pool. At most one job per subject is active (`ErrSubjectBusy`).
- `fn` must honour `ctx` (cancelled by `Cancel` and by shutdown) and write human-readable progress and full error output to `log`. The `detail` shown to clients is empty on success, the message of a `jobs.Fail(msg, cause)` error, or a generic message; panics are recovered into `error`.
- Status transitions are persisted (`queued`, `running`, then `success`, `error` or `cancelled`); final writes use a background context so they survive shutdown.
- `Done(id)` closes when the job leaves this process; the log follow endpoint uses it to end streams.
- Job kinds and subject types are listed in `internal/apitypes/jobs.go`; add new ones there.
- Verify with `go test ./internal/jobs/... ./internal/httpapi/...`.
